<span id="A1.T3.3.11.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.T3.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{ij}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\tau^{2}/d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{ij}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\tau^{2}/d)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.T3.3.11.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">,  </span><math id="A1.T3.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Z}}=\theta\,{\bm{u}}{\bm{v}}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒁</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒗</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Z}}=\theta\,{\bm{u}}{\bm{v}}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T3.3.11.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A1.T3.3.11.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:48.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.3.11.4.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.3.11.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Sec. 2</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.3.12" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T3.3.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A1.T3.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{{\bm{\varepsilon}}},\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝜺</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">ε</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{{\bm{\varepsilon}}},\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T3.3.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="A1.T3.3.12.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:165.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.3.12.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.3.12.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Label noise and its variance</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T3.3.12.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="A1.T3.3.12.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:102.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.3.12.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.3.12.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">IID, </span><math id="A1.T3.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0,\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">ε</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0,\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T3.3.12.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="A1.T3.3.12.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:48.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.3.12.4.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.3.12.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Sec. 2</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Glossary of recurrent parameters and symbols. All <math id="A1.T3.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(1)</annotation></semantics></math> constants are independent of <math id="A1.T3.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n,d</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Other Notations. </h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use lowercase <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>, lowercase bold <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{a}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒂</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{a}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and uppercase bold <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> letters to denote scalars, vectors, and matrices respectively. We use <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the Euclidean norm if the argument is a vector and the operator norm if the argument is a matrix. We use <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the Frobenius norm. When slicing one entry from a vector or matrix, we use both <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{a}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{a}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>, where the latter intends to emphasize the source of the scalar.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Non-Linear Experiment</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We used 500 data points in 750 dimensional space, with a hidden width of 1000. We used full batch gradient descent for 100 epochs with a learning rate of 1e-4. Each data point is averaged over 50 trials. Equal Frobenius norm scaling was used for the size of the spike.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Spike Recovery Case</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider the special case where the goal is to recover the spike direction <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒖</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{u}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In this setting, the target <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> depends only on the spike component <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒁</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Z}}</annotation></semantics></math>, with no contribution from the noise <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{A}=\tilde{\alpha}_{A}=0,\qquad\alpha_{Z}=\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}=\alpha&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{A}=\tilde{\alpha}_{A}=0,\qquad\alpha_{Z}=\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}=\alpha&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, the target <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> is proportional to the signal <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒁</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Z}}</annotation></semantics></math> plus possible observation noise <math id="A3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\varepsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\varepsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Equal Operator Norm</h5>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this regime, we have that the risk is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{c&lt;1}=\frac{\gamma\alpha_{Z}^{2}\tau^{2}}{(1-c)(\gamma+1)}({\bm{\beta}}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+\frac{c}{1-c}\tau^{2}_{\varepsilon},\qquad\mathcal{R}_{c&gt;1}=\frac{\gamma c(c^{2}+\gamma)\alpha_{Z}^{2}\tau^{2}}{(c-1)(\gamma+c)^{2}}({\bm{\beta}}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+\frac{1}{c-1}\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{c&lt;1}=\frac{\gamma\alpha_{Z}^{2}\tau^{2}}{(1-c)(\gamma+1)}({\bm{\beta}}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+\frac{c}{1-c}\tau^{2}_{\varepsilon},\qquad\mathcal{R}_{c&gt;1}=\frac{\gamma c(c^{2}+\gamma)\alpha_{Z}^{2}\tau^{2}}{(c-1)(\gamma+c)^{2}}({\bm{\beta}}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+\frac{1}{c-1}\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here again, we see that when <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\Theta_{c}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\Theta_{c}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have tempered overfitting and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{c}(1)\leq\gamma\leq o_{c}(c^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{c}(1)\leq\gamma\leq o_{c}(c^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have catastrophic overfitting and for <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\Omega_{c}(c^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\Omega_{c}(c^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> we get tempered overfitting again.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Equal Frobenius Norm</h5>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">. In this regime, we have that</p>
<table id="A3.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{c&lt;1}=\frac{\alpha_{Z}^{2}\tau^{2}}{1-c}({\bm{\beta}}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+\frac{c}{1-c}\tau^{2}_{\varepsilon}\quad R_{c&gt;1}=\frac{c\alpha_{Z}^{2}\tau^{2}}{c-1}({\bm{\beta}}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+\frac{1}{c-1}\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{c&lt;1}=\frac{\alpha_{Z}^{2}\tau^{2}}{1-c}({\bm{\beta}}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+\frac{c}{1-c}\tau^{2}_{\varepsilon}\quad R_{c&gt;1}=\frac{c\alpha_{Z}^{2}\tau^{2}}{c-1}({\bm{\beta}}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+\frac{1}{c-1}\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This generalizes the spike recovery setting studied in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>, which assumed noiseless targets (<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\varepsilon}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\varepsilon}=0</annotation></semantics></math>) and the equal Frobenius norm scaling. Our formula allows for observation noise and thus captures the more realistic case where the target <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> itself contains randomness not aligned with the spike. Here we see that we have tempered overfitting unless <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{2}=o(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{2}=o(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the case considered in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5 (Generalization Risk). ‣ 3.4 General Theorem ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a></h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5 (Generalization Risk). ‣ 3.4 General Theorem ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>
In particular, as <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n,d\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n,d\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d/n\to c\in(0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d/n\to c\in(0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the following expressions for each term. 
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bias:</span> For <math id="A4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that the bias term is</p>
<table id="A4.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\theta}^{2}\left[({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}+(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})+\frac{\tau^{2}}{\theta^{2}+\tau^{2}}\right)^{2}+\tau^{2}_{\varepsilon}\frac{c}{1-c}\frac{1}{d(\theta^{2}+\tau^{2})}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\theta}^{2}\left[({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}+(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})+\frac{\tau^{2}}{\theta^{2}+\tau^{2}}\right)^{2}+\tau^{2}_{\varepsilon}\frac{c}{1-c}\frac{1}{d(\theta^{2}+\tau^{2})}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we that the bias term is</p>
<table id="A4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\theta}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}+\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)\frac{\tau^{2}c}{\theta^{2}+\tau^{2}c}\right)^{2}+\tilde{\theta}^{2}\left[\alpha_{A}^{2}\frac{\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}}{d}\frac{c-1}{c}\frac{\theta^{2}\tau^{2}c}{(\theta^{2}+\tau^{2}c)^{2}}+\tau^{2}_{\varepsilon}\frac{c}{c-1}\frac{\theta^{2}+\tau^{2}}{n(\theta^{2}+\tau^{2}c)^{2}}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\theta}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}+\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)\frac{\tau^{2}c}{\theta^{2}+\tau^{2}c}\right)^{2}+\tilde{\theta}^{2}\left[\alpha_{A}^{2}\frac{\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}}{d}\frac{c-1}{c}\frac{\theta^{2}\tau^{2}c}{(\theta^{2}+\tau^{2}c)^{2}}+\tau^{2}_{\varepsilon}\frac{c}{c-1}\frac{\theta^{2}+\tau^{2}}{n(\theta^{2}+\tau^{2}c)^{2}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Variance:</span> For <math id="A4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that the variance term is</p>
<table id="A4.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha_{A}^{2}\tilde{\tau}^{2}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}+\tilde{\tau}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left[\frac{1}{1-c}\frac{\theta^{4}+\theta^{2}\tau^{2}c}{(\theta^{2}+\tau^{2})^{2}}\left(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A}\right)^{2}+2\alpha_{A}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\frac{\theta^{2}}{\theta^{2}+\tau^{2}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha_{A}^{2}\tilde{\tau}^{2}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}+\tilde{\tau}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left[\frac{1}{1-c}\frac{\theta^{4}+\theta^{2}\tau^{2}c}{(\theta^{2}+\tau^{2})^{2}}\left(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A}\right)^{2}+2\alpha_{A}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\frac{\theta^{2}}{\theta^{2}+\tau^{2}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\tau^{2}_{\varepsilon}\frac{\tilde{\tau}^{2}}{\tau^{2}}\left[\frac{c}{1-c}-\frac{\theta^{2}}{d(\theta^{2}+\tau^{2})}\,\frac{c}{1-c}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\tau^{2}_{\varepsilon}\frac{\tilde{\tau}^{2}}{\tau^{2}}\left[\frac{c}{1-c}-\frac{\theta^{2}}{d(\theta^{2}+\tau^{2})}\,\frac{c}{1-c}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that the variance term is</p>
<table id="A4.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\tau}^{2}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}\left(\frac{\alpha_{A}^{2}}{c}-\frac{\alpha_{A}^{2}}{d}\frac{\theta^{2}}{\theta^{2}+\tau^{2}c}\right)+\tilde{\tau}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\frac{c}{(c-1)}\frac{\theta^{2}}{\theta^{2}+\tau^{2}c}\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\tau}^{2}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}\left(\frac{\alpha_{A}^{2}}{c}-\frac{\alpha_{A}^{2}}{d}\frac{\theta^{2}}{\theta^{2}+\tau^{2}c}\right)+\tilde{\tau}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\frac{c}{(c-1)}\frac{\theta^{2}}{\theta^{2}+\tau^{2}c}\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}\frac{\tilde{\tau}^{2}}{\tau^{2}}\left(\frac{1}{c-1}-\frac{\theta^{2}}{d(\theta^{2}+\tau^{2}c)}\frac{c}{c-1}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}\frac{\tilde{\tau}^{2}}{\tau^{2}}\left(\frac{1}{c-1}-\frac{\theta^{2}}{d(\theta^{2}+\tau^{2}c)}\frac{c}{c-1}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Data Noise:</span> For all <math id="A4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\alpha}_{A}^{2}\tilde{\tau}^{2}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\alpha}_{A}^{2}\tilde{\tau}^{2}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Target Alignment:</span> For <math id="A4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that the alignment term is</p>
<table id="A4.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-2\tilde{\alpha}_{A}\tilde{\tau}^{2}\left((\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\frac{\theta^{2}}{\theta^{2}+\tau^{2}}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+\alpha_{A}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2\tilde{\alpha}_{A}\tilde{\tau}^{2}\left((\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\frac{\theta^{2}}{\theta^{2}+\tau^{2}}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+\alpha_{A}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that the alignment term is</p>
<table id="A4.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-2\tilde{\alpha}_{A}\tilde{\tau}^{2}\left(\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)\frac{\theta^{2}}{\theta^{2}+\tau^{2}c}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+\alpha_{A}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}\left(\frac{1}{c}-\frac{1}{d}\,\frac{\theta^{2}}{\theta^{2}+\tau^{2}c}\right)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2\tilde{\alpha}_{A}\tilde{\tau}^{2}\left(\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)\frac{\theta^{2}}{\theta^{2}+\tau^{2}c}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+\alpha_{A}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}\left(\frac{1}{c}-\frac{1}{d}\,\frac{\theta^{2}}{\theta^{2}+\tau^{2}c}\right)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Error terms:</span> The largest error terms for all <math id="A4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> are:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)=o(1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)=o(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Remark:</h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We note that the above theorem is very general and captures all of the theorems in the main text as special cases. It is worth noting that the theorem also incorporates different signal and bulk strengths for test data, namely for <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The proof will be broken up into roughly 6 steps</p>
<ol id="A4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rescale the problem</span> To apply standard results we rescale the problem. Section <a href="#A4.SS1" title="D.1 Step 0: Rescaling ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Decompose the error into four terms.</span> We shall refer to these terms as the 1) bias, 2) variance, 3) data noise, and 4) target alignment. Section <a href="#A4.SS2" title="D.2 Step 1: Decompose Error ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Simplify the expressions.</span> We shall then use the result from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite> to simplify the expression for each of the four terms. In particular, we shall express each term as the product of dependent functions of the eigenvalues of <math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Section <a href="#A4.SS3" title="D.3 Step 2: Simplifying Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Random matrix theory estimate.</span> We then use standard results from random matrix theory such as <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, <a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> to obtain a closed-form formula of the building blocks for the risk. Section <a href="#A4.SS4" title="D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bound Products</span>. We then show that products of our building blocks concentrate. Step 4 (Section <a href="#A4.SS5" title="D.5 Step 4: Bounding the Expectation of Products of Dependent Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.5</span></a>) then collects the final terms.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">6.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Undo Scaling</span> Step 5 (Section <a href="#A4.SS6" title="D.6 Step 5: Upscaling and Asymptotic Risk Formulas ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.6</span></a>) gives us back the correct scaling.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Section <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Probability Lemmas ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a> has some generic probability lemmas that we need.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Step 0: Rescaling</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In order to better align with existing results and use them accordingly, we change our scalings for now and switch back after our derivation. That is, we divide everything by <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, we shall use</p>
<table id="A4.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\theta}{\sqrt{d}}{\bm{u}}{\bm{w}}^{\top}=\theta\frac{\|{\bm{w}}\|}{\sqrt{d}}{\bm{u}}\frac{{\bm{w}}^{\top}}{\|{\bm{w}}\|}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>θ</mi><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\theta}{\sqrt{d}}{\bm{u}}{\bm{w}}^{\top}=\theta\frac{\|{\bm{w}}\|}{\sqrt{d}}{\bm{u}}\frac{{\bm{w}}^{\top}}{\|{\bm{w}}\|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">as the spike. We shall let</p>
<table id="A4.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{2}:=\theta^{2}\frac{\|{\bm{w}}\|^{2}}{d}\quad\text{ and }\quad{\bm{v}}:=\frac{{\bm{w}}^{\top}}{\|{\bm{w}}\|}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext> and </mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{2}:=\theta^{2}\frac{\|{\bm{w}}\|^{2}}{d}\quad\text{ and }\quad{\bm{v}}:=\frac{{\bm{w}}^{\top}}{\|{\bm{w}}\|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Here, we treat <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}</annotation></semantics></math> as fixed unit norm vector and our spike is</p>
<table id="A4.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Z}}_{r}:=\eta{\bm{u}}{\bm{v}}^{T}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Z}}_{r}:=\eta{\bm{u}}{\bm{v}}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> noise after dividing by <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A4.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}_{r}:=\frac{\tau}{\sqrt{d}}N" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>τ</mi><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}_{r}:=\frac{\tau}{\sqrt{d}}N</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> are mean zero variance 1 entries. Here the appendix, we shall use the letter <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally let</p>
<table id="A4.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{X}}_{r}={\bm{Z}}_{r}+{\bm{A}}_{r}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{X}}_{r}={\bm{Z}}_{r}+{\bm{A}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">We can note that <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\beta}}_{int}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\beta}}_{int}</annotation></semantics></math>, is still the solution to</p>
<table id="A4.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\frac{{\bm{y}}}{\sqrt{d}}-{\bm{\beta}}^{\top}{\bm{X}}_{r}\right\|^{2},\quad\text{where }\ \frac{{\bm{y}}}{\sqrt{d}}={\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}({\bm{Z}}_{r}+{\bm{A}}_{r})+\frac{{\bm{\varepsilon}}}{\sqrt{d}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>𝒚</mi><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>where </mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>𝒚</mi><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>𝜺</mi><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\frac{{\bm{y}}}{\sqrt{d}}-{\bm{\beta}}^{\top}{\bm{X}}_{r}\right\|^{2},\quad\text{where }\ \frac{{\bm{y}}}{\sqrt{d}}={\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}({\bm{Z}}_{r}+{\bm{A}}_{r})+\frac{{\bm{\varepsilon}}}{\sqrt{d}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.7" class="ltx_p">We define</p>
<table id="A4.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{{\bm{\varepsilon}}}{\sqrt{d}}=:{\bm{\varepsilon}}_{r}\sim\mathcal{N}\left(0,\frac{\tau^{2}_{\varepsilon}}{d}\right),\quad\tau^{2}_{\varepsilon,r}:=\frac{\tau^{2}_{\varepsilon}}{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>𝜺</mi><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜺</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{{\bm{\varepsilon}}}{\sqrt{d}}=:{\bm{\varepsilon}}_{r}\sim\mathcal{N}\left(0,\frac{\tau^{2}_{\varepsilon}}{d}\right),\quad\tau^{2}_{\varepsilon,r}:=\frac{\tau^{2}_{\varepsilon}}{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.8" class="ltx_p">Then when we want to test, we shall look at the rescaled error</p>
<table id="A4.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\tilde{n}}\left\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}_{r}+\tilde{\alpha}_{A}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}_{r})-{\bm{\beta}}_{int}^{\top}(\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}_{r}+\tilde{{\bm{A}}}_{r})\right\|_{F}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\tilde{n}}\left\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}_{r}+\tilde{\alpha}_{A}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}_{r})-{\bm{\beta}}_{int}^{\top}(\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}_{r}+\tilde{{\bm{A}}}_{r})\right\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="53.77" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 650 53.77" width="650"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,53.77) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 47.87 C 0 51.13 2.64 53.77 5.91 53.77 L 644.09 53.77 C 647.36 53.77 650 51.13 650 47.87 L 650 5.91 C 650 2.64 647.36 0 644.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 47.87 C 1.97 50.04 3.73 51.8 5.91 51.8 L 644.09 51.8 C 646.27 51.8 648.03 50.04 648.03 47.87 L 648.03 5.91 C 648.03 3.73 646.27 1.97 644.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 13.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:43.85em;--ltx-fo-height:1.89em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="26.21" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 26.21)" width="606.76"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:43.85em;">
<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Through Steps 1 - 4, we shall drop the subscript<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <math id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Step 1: Decompose Error</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Using the fact that <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\bm{A}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\bm{A}}}</annotation></semantics></math> has been zero entries and is independent of <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we see that we can decompose the error as follows. Again here we consider <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{n}</annotation></semantics></math> samples of test data and take the average (in expectation, this is the same as one test point).</p>
<table id="A4.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\tilde{n}}\left\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}(\tilde{\alpha}_{z}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}+\tilde{\alpha}_{A}\tilde{{\bm{A}}})-{\bm{\beta}}_{int}^{\top}(\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}+\tilde{{\bm{A}}})\right\|_{F}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\tilde{n}}\left\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}(\tilde{\alpha}_{z}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}+\tilde{\alpha}_{A}\tilde{{\bm{A}}})-{\bm{\beta}}_{int}^{\top}(\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}+\tilde{{\bm{A}}})\right\|_{F}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\tilde{n}}\left\|\tilde{\alpha}_{z}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}-{\bm{\beta}}_{int}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}\right\|_{F}^{2}\right]+\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\tilde{n}}\left\|\tilde{\alpha}_{A}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}-{\bm{\beta}}_{int}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}\right\|_{F}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\tilde{n}}\left\|\tilde{\alpha}_{z}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}-{\bm{\beta}}_{int}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}\right\|_{F}^{2}\right]+\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\tilde{n}}\left\|\tilde{\alpha}_{A}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}-{\bm{\beta}}_{int}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}\right\|_{F}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\underbrace{\frac{1}{\tilde{n}}\left\|\tilde{\alpha}_{z}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}-{\bm{\beta}}_{int}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}\right\|_{F}^{2}}_{\text{Bias}}+\underbrace{\frac{1}{\tilde{n}}\left\|{\bm{\beta}}_{int}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}\right\|_{F}^{2}}_{\text{Variance}}+\underbrace{\frac{1}{\tilde{n}}\tilde{\alpha}_{A}^{2}\left\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}\right\|_{F}^{2}}_{\text{Data Noise}}+\underbrace{\left(-\frac{2}{\tilde{n}}\tilde{\alpha}_{A}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{int}\right)}_{\text{Target Alignment}}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Bias</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Variance</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Data Noise</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Target Alignment</mtext></munder></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\underbrace{\frac{1}{\tilde{n}}\left\|\tilde{\alpha}_{z}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}-{\bm{\beta}}_{int}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}\right\|_{F}^{2}}_{\text{Bias}}+\underbrace{\frac{1}{\tilde{n}}\left\|{\bm{\beta}}_{int}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}\right\|_{F}^{2}}_{\text{Variance}}+\underbrace{\frac{1}{\tilde{n}}\tilde{\alpha}_{A}^{2}\left\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}\right\|_{F}^{2}}_{\text{Data Noise}}+\underbrace{\left(-\frac{2}{\tilde{n}}\tilde{\alpha}_{A}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{int}\right)}_{\text{Target Alignment}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We compute these four terms one by one in the following sections.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Step 2: Simplifying Terms</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section simplifies the four terms. We begin by recalling results from prior work. We state them here for completeness.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 6</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Theorems 3, 5 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite>)<span id="Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Define the following helper functions <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{h}}={\bm{v}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐡</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{h}}={\bm{v}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{k}}={\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{k}}={\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{u}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{t}}={\bm{v}}^{\top}({\bm{I}}-{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{A}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐀</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{t}}={\bm{v}}^{\top}({\bm{I}}-{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{A}})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi=1+\eta{\bm{v}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi=1+\eta{\bm{v}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{u}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}=({\bm{I}}-{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}){\bm{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}=({\bm{I}}-{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}){\bm{u}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1}=\eta^{2}\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}+\xi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐭</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐤</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1}=\eta^{2}\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}+\xi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{2}=\eta^{2}\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}+\xi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐡</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{2}=\eta^{2}\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}+\xi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{p}}_{1}=-\frac{\eta^{2}\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}}{\xi}{\bm{t}}^{\top}-\eta{\bm{k}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒕</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒌</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{p}}_{1}=-\frac{\eta^{2}\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}}{\xi}{\bm{t}}^{\top}-\eta{\bm{k}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{q}}_{1}^{\top}=-\frac{\eta\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}}{\xi}{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}-{\bm{h}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒌</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒉</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{q}}_{1}^{\top}=-\frac{\eta\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}}{\xi}{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}-{\bm{h}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{p}}_{2}=-\frac{\eta^{2}\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}}{\xi}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}-\eta{\bm{k}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒌</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{p}}_{2}=-\frac{\eta^{2}\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}}{\xi}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}-\eta{\bm{k}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex41.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{q}}_{2}^{\top}=-\frac{\eta\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}}{\xi}{\bm{s}}^{\top}-{\bm{h}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒉</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{q}}_{2}^{\top}=-\frac{\eta\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}}{\xi}{\bm{s}}^{\top}-{\bm{h}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then we have that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}=\begin{cases}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}+\frac{\eta}{\xi}{\bm{t}}^{\top}{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}-\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{1}}{\bm{p}}_{1}{\bm{q}}_{1}^{\top},\quad c&lt;1\\
{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}+\frac{\eta}{\xi}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{s}}^{\top}-\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{p}}_{2}{\bm{q}}_{2}^{\top},\quad c&gt;1\end{cases}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mi>ξ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒕</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒌</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mi>ξ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}=\begin{cases}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}+\frac{\eta}{\xi}{\bm{t}}^{\top}{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}-\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{1}}{\bm{p}}_{1}{\bm{q}}_{1}^{\top},\quad c&lt;1\\
{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}+\frac{\eta}{\xi}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{s}}^{\top}-\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{p}}_{2}{\bm{q}}_{2}^{\top},\quad c&gt;1\end{cases}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The following subsections - Bias <a href="#A4.SS3.SSS1" title="D.3.1 Bias ‣ D.3 Step 2: Simplifying Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3.1</span></a>, Variance <a href="#A4.SS3.SSS2" title="D.3.2 Variance ‣ D.3 Step 2: Simplifying Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3.2</span></a>, Data Noise <a href="#A4.SS3.SSS3" title="D.3.3 Data Noise ‣ D.3 Step 2: Simplifying Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3.3</span></a>, and Target Alignment <a href="#A4.SS3.SSS4" title="D.3.4 Target Alignment ‣ D.3 Step 2: Simplifying Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3.4</span></a> - present the linear algebraic simplifications of the results. To derive this results. We shall need some helper results that are presented in Section <a href="#A4.SS3.SSS5" title="D.3.5 Helper Lemmas ‣ D.3 Step 2: Simplifying Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3.5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.3.1 </span>Bias</h4>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Using <a href="#Thmlemma5" title="Lemma 5 (Bias Term). ‣ D.3.5 Helper Lemmas ‣ D.3 Step 2: Simplifying Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we have that if <math id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A4.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\alpha}_{z}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}-{\bm{\beta}}_{int}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}=\left[\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{1}}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\right]{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}+\frac{\tilde{\eta}}{\eta}\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{1}}{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}{\bm{p}}_{1}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝜺</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\alpha}_{z}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}-{\bm{\beta}}_{int}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}=\left[\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{1}}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\right]{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}+\frac{\tilde{\eta}}{\eta}\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{1}}{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}{\bm{p}}_{1}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and if <math id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A4.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\alpha}_{z}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}-{\bm{\beta}}_{int}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}={\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}){\bm{I}}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger})\right]\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}-\alpha_{A}\frac{\eta\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{u}}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}+\frac{\tilde{\eta}}{\eta}\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}{\bm{p}}_{2}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝜺</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\alpha}_{z}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}-{\bm{\beta}}_{int}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}={\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}){\bm{I}}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger})\right]\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}-\alpha_{A}\frac{\eta\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{u}}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}+\frac{\tilde{\eta}}{\eta}\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}{\bm{p}}_{2}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The bias equals the expected squared norm of this term (divided by <math id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{n}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.3.2 </span>Variance</h4>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma8" title="Lemma 8 (Preliminary Expansion of Variance). ‣ D.3.5 Helper Lemmas ‣ D.3 Step 2: Simplifying Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> gives us that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 10.0pt\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\tilde{n}}\left\|{\bm{\beta}}_{int}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}\right\|_{F}^{2}\right]=\mathbb{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 10.0pt\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\tilde{n}}\left\|{\bm{\beta}}_{int}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}\right\|_{F}^{2}\right]=\mathbb{E}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex45.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left[\frac{\tilde{\tau}^{2}\alpha_{z}^{2}}{d}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{Z}}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{Z}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}+\frac{\tilde{\tau}^{2}\alpha_{A}^{2}}{d}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{A}}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mi>𝒁</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mi>𝒁</mi><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left[\frac{\tilde{\tau}^{2}\alpha_{z}^{2}}{d}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{Z}}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{Z}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}+\frac{\tilde{\tau}^{2}\alpha_{A}^{2}}{d}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{A}}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left.+\frac{2\tilde{\tau}^{2}\alpha_{A}\alpha_{z}}{d}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{Z}}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}+\frac{\tilde{\tau}^{2}}{d}{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{\varepsilon}}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mi>𝒁</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mi>𝜺</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mi>𝜺</mi><mo>]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left.+\frac{2\tilde{\tau}^{2}\alpha_{A}\alpha_{z}}{d}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{Z}}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}+\frac{\tilde{\tau}^{2}}{d}{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{\varepsilon}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.3.3 </span>Data Noise</h4>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The data noise term is the simplest to understand. Preliminary calculation gives us:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\tilde{n}}\tilde{\alpha}_{A}^{2}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{A}}\left[\left\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}\right\|_{F}^{2}\right]=\frac{\tilde{\alpha}_{A}^{2}}{\tilde{n}}\frac{\tilde{\rho}^{2}\tilde{n}}{d}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}=\frac{\tilde{\alpha}_{A}^{2}\tilde{\rho}^{2}}{d}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\tilde{n}}\tilde{\alpha}_{A}^{2}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{A}}\left[\left\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}\right\|_{F}^{2}\right]=\frac{\tilde{\alpha}_{A}^{2}}{\tilde{n}}\frac{\tilde{\rho}^{2}\tilde{n}}{d}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}=\frac{\tilde{\alpha}_{A}^{2}\tilde{\rho}^{2}}{d}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.3.4 </span>Target Alignment</h4>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To understand this term, we first note that <math id="A4.SS3.SSS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\bm{A}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\bm{A}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of everything else. Hence we replace <math id="A4.SS3.SSS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\bm{A}}}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\bm{A}}}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> with its expectation <math id="A4.SS3.SSS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\tilde{\rho}^{2}\tilde{n}}{d}{\bm{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\tilde{\rho}^{2}\tilde{n}}{d}{\bm{I}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A4.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{A}}\left[-\frac{2}{\tilde{n}}\tilde{\alpha}_{A}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{int}\right]=-\frac{2}{\tilde{n}}\frac{\tilde{\rho}^{2}\tilde{n}}{d}\tilde{\alpha}_{A}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{int}=-\frac{2\tilde{\alpha}_{A}\tilde{\rho}^{2}}{d}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{int}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{A}}\left[-\frac{2}{\tilde{n}}\tilde{\alpha}_{A}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{int}\right]=-\frac{2}{\tilde{n}}\frac{\tilde{\rho}^{2}\tilde{n}}{d}\tilde{\alpha}_{A}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{int}=-\frac{2\tilde{\alpha}_{A}\tilde{\rho}^{2}}{d}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{int}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A4.SS3.SSS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\varepsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\varepsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math> has mean-zero entries that are independent of everything else. We see that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\varepsilon}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{int}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\varepsilon}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{int}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\varepsilon}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\left((\alpha_{z}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{Z}}+{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top})({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}+\alpha_{A}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{A}}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}\right)^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒁</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝜺</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\varepsilon}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\left((\alpha_{z}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{Z}}+{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top})({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}+\alpha_{A}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{A}}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}\right)^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\left(\alpha_{z}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{Z}}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{A}}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\left(\alpha_{z}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{Z}}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{A}}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha_{z}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{Z}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}+\alpha_{A}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha_{z}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{Z}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}+\alpha_{A}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS5" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.3.5 </span>Helper Lemmas</h4>

<div id="Thmprop1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmprop1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 1</span></span><span id="Thmprop1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Proposition 2 from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>)<span id="Thmprop1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmprop1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmprop1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmprop1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In the setting from Section <a href="#S2" title="2 Problem Setting ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Z}}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}=\begin{cases}\frac{\eta\xi}{\gamma_{1}}{\bm{u}}{\bm{h}}+\frac{\eta^{2}\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}{\bm{u}}{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger},\quad c&lt;1\\
\frac{\eta\xi}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{u}}{\bm{h}}+\frac{\eta^{2}\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{u}}{\bm{s}}^{\top},\quad c&gt;1\end{cases}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒉</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒌</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒉</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Z}}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}=\begin{cases}\frac{\eta\xi}{\gamma_{1}}{\bm{u}}{\bm{h}}+\frac{\eta^{2}\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}{\bm{u}}{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger},\quad c&lt;1\\
\frac{\eta\xi}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{u}}{\bm{h}}+\frac{\eta^{2}\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{u}}{\bm{s}}^{\top},\quad c&gt;1\end{cases}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> has full rank, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}=\begin{cases}-\frac{\tilde{\eta}\xi}{\eta\gamma_{1}}{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}{\bm{p}}_{1}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}&amp;c&lt;1\\
-\frac{\tilde{\eta}\xi}{\eta\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}{\bm{p}}_{2}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}&amp;c&gt;1\end{cases}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝜺</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝜺</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝜺</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}=\begin{cases}-\frac{\tilde{\eta}\xi}{\eta\gamma_{1}}{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}{\bm{p}}_{1}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}&amp;c&lt;1\\
-\frac{\tilde{\eta}\xi}{\eta\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}{\bm{p}}_{2}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}&amp;c&gt;1\end{cases}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.SSS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">After substitutions, <a href="#Thmprop1" title="Proposition 1 (Proposition 2 from []). ‣ D.3.5 Helper Lemmas ‣ D.3 Step 2: Simplifying Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> implies that for <math id="A4.SS3.SSS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS3.SSS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝜺</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}</annotation></semantics></math> becomes:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}\left({\bm{A}}^{\dagger}+\frac{\eta}{\xi}{\bm{t}}^{\top}{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}-\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{1}}{\bm{p}}_{1}\left(-\frac{\eta\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}}{\xi}{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}-{\bm{h}}\right)\right)\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝜺</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mi>ξ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒕</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒌</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒌</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒉</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}\left({\bm{A}}^{\dagger}+\frac{\eta}{\xi}{\bm{t}}^{\top}{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}-\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{1}}{\bm{p}}_{1}\left(-\frac{\eta\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}}{\xi}{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}-{\bm{h}}\right)\right)\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\hskip 2.84544pt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\hskip 2.84544pt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex52.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\eta}{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}\left({\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{u}}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}+\frac{\eta}{\xi}{\bm{t}}^{\top}{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{u}}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}-\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{1}}{\bm{p}}_{1}\left(-\frac{\eta\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}}{\xi}{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{u}}-{\bm{h}}{\bm{u}}\right)\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}\right)\quad\text{by $\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}=\tilde{\eta}{\bm{u}}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}$}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝜺</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mi>ξ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒕</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒌</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒌</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>by </mtext><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\eta}{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}\left({\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{u}}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}+\frac{\eta}{\xi}{\bm{t}}^{\top}{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{u}}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}-\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{1}}{\bm{p}}_{1}\left(-\frac{\eta\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}}{\xi}{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{u}}-{\bm{h}}{\bm{u}}\right)\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}\right)\quad\text{by $\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}=\tilde{\eta}{\bm{u}}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}$}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.SSS5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A4.SS3.SSS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{k}}={\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒌</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{k}}={\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{u}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.SSS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{h}}{\bm{u}}={\bm{v}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{u}}=\frac{\xi-1}{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{h}}{\bm{u}}={\bm{v}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{u}}=\frac{\xi-1}{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, we then have that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
